OL,3,GNEWSAHomes set to go ahead despite
OL,4,Aenvironmental fears
OL,5,
OL,6,FFive objections have been made to the
OL,7,Fdevelopment over the loss of wildlife
OL,8,Fhabitats and the impact on nearby
OL,9,Fnature reserves, but a planning
OL,10,Fofficer's report said the development
OL,11,Fwas "considered to be acceptable in
OL,12,Fprinciple" subject to the imposition of
OL,13,Fcertain conditions.
